    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the build is green (the single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, passes; the other two files are test helpers, not test classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change de-duplicates a new owner's `customerCode` against existing owners before saving.\n\n**`OwnerCustomerCodes.java`** \u2014 added a focused `deduplicate(base, taken)` helper alongside the existing formatting methods. It returns `base` when free, otherwise the first `base-<n>` (starting at n=2) not already taken. This keeps the \"customer code\" rules together while staying a distinct, single-purpose method.\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now injects `OwnerRepository` (the same pattern as sibling steps like `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`), collects the non-null `customerCode`s of existing owners, and stores the de-duplicated result. Since this step runs before `save`, `findAll()` never includes the new owner itself.\n\nThe de-dup logic lives in the code-formatting class; the function class stays a thin orchestrator that reads existing state and applies the result \u2014 no class became a catch-all, and the existing `forOwner`/`format`/`hash8` code is reused unchanged.",
